; case: time-horizon
; verdict: accept
; ambiguous: no
; tests: externality=pass implementation-independence=pass non-prescription=pass
; rationale: States an externally testable guarantee about observed time. Any timer that keeps
;   observations unambiguous for 60 s satisfies it, whatever its width or rate.
; other-side: engine: wrap handling, epoch extension, read frequency, the arithmetic, and the
;   proof that the requirement is met
;
(defservice time.monotonic
  (requires
    (unambiguous-horizon (at-least 60 s))))
